  "id": "COMPOUND:25003 - PROTEIN:6271",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and Lysosomal Pro-X carboxypeptidase, mediated through palmarumycin CP18. This compound appears to act as a bridge, with multiple pathways linking the acid to the enzyme. Path_19051 and Path_19053 both indicate that the acid targets A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18, and that this compound further targets the lysosomal enzyme. Path_19052 adds an alternative route, where the acid targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of Mollicellin N, also leading to the same enzyme. These findings collectively suggest that the acid may influence the enzyme through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving distinct pathways or targets. The evidence supports a complex network of interactions, where the acid may modulate the enzyme through various intermediaries, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
